        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: prioritize exhausted Antigravity quota in menu bar and highest usage",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- keep exhausted Antigravity five-hour or weekly quota buckets visible instead of falling back to a less-constrained lane\n- make automatic menu-bar display and cross-provider highest-usage ranking use the same most-constrained recognized quota window\n- when tied windows have reset timestamps, prefer the nearest future reset and deprioritize elapsed resets\n- recognize the supported five-hour cadence spellings while ignoring unknown future cadences\n\n## Why\n\nThe menu bar should show the quota lane that actually blocks work. Selecting a lower-used or already-expired lane can hide both an exhausted family and its actionable reset countdown.\n\n## Scope\n\n- five production/test files\n- no account, authentication, provider-fetching, or unrelated platform-test changes\n\n## Validation\n\n- `swift test --filter 'MenuBarMetricWindowResolverTests|UsageStoreHighestUsageTests'`\n- SwiftFormat on all changed Swift sources and tests\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n\nThe production resolver and highest-usage consumer now agree on the same Antigravity quota percentage; reset ordering is only a tie-breaker between equally constrained lanes.\n",
